da034a3","position":"1785399452272296170-4bc4471d-404b-44b2-b193-3a53195749ce"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"c3ea939ddb0e2f5de99ac139faabc0546d9d59cf12a017d73179220cee4d4a67","event_uuid":"5461fd5a-0ea2-40f5-baae-1708f9d813a7","position":{"commit_sha":"c1dc072b60862a7ed8f8cc71f107416dae950b36","position":"1785399833113505001-5461fd5a-0ea2-40f5-baae-1708f9d813a7"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-220_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"d1ad70ed-ce91-4b63-9f32-e6b36aea17d4","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation complete in worktree tok-s3: edit --review (valueless flag, post-commit signed review, disposition exit codes) + claim --review (two-stage sensing via new gates._plan_review_gate_applies + llm.claim_gate_check; claim only on PASS; not cascaded). 21 new tests in tests/unit/test_review_flags.py; lint/typecheck/related suites green. Pushed as Gerrit change 1036 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1036); awaiting LLM-Review + Verified.","timestamp":1785399833113505001}],"created_at":1785384352183857001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"46b14328-83c1-4b79-9a93-a00cc540ced3","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"d33d-bf91-2086-4b40"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe edit-then-re-review loop is common and hazardous as two shell commands, and claim's recovery text (src/rebar/_commands/gates.py:213-215) tells the user to run review-plan then claim by hand. Operator approved both flags. OSS precedent favors embedding prerequisite verification in the consuming verb (cargo publish verifies by default; terraform apply consumes a staleness-checked plan artifact) over new fused commands.\n\n## Approach\n(1) `rebar edit <id> ... --review`: edit_cli's hand-rolled parser (src/rebar/_commands/composer.py:528-561) treats every --name as requiring a value, so `--review` is handled as an explicit valueless flag checked BEFORE the field loop (popped from argv, bypassing the --key=value pathway); after edit_core commits the EDIT event, invoke rebar.llm.review_plan(ticket_id, sign=True) and map the returned verdict dict to the process exit status with the disposition mapping (0 PASS / 1 BLOCK / 2 INDETERMINATE / 11 retryable per ADR 0040). _disposition_exit_code stays in src/rebar/_cli/_llm_commands.py; the flag handlers use a lazy in-function import (`from rebar._cli._llm_commands import _disposition_exit_code`) — the established pattern for a _commands module reaching a _cli helper, per the existing lazy `from rebar._cli import _help` inside reopen_cli at src/rebar/_commands/transition.py:562. No file moves. (2) `rebar claim <id> --review`: implemented as a new keyword parameter review: bool = False on claim_compute, threaded from claim_cli's parser; the logic sits inside claim_compute at the claim.py:133 seam: when --review is set and the gate applies, call llm.claim_gate_check(ticket_id); if it reports not-ok, run review_plan(sign=True). The review verdict then determines control flow exactly: on PASS, proceed into the normal plan_review_precheck path and claim (precheck re-checks and fails closed with the standard message if the attestation is somehow still stale); on BLOCK, INDETERMINATE, or a retryable degrade, the claim is NOT attempted — the command prints the review's finding summary and exits with the disposition mapping applied to the review result (1 / 2 / 11 respectively), leaving the ticket open for revision. When stage 1 says the gate does not apply (disabled or exempt type), --review prints a one-line notice \"plan-review gate not enabled for this ticket; --review skipped\" and the claim proceeds — never a silent no-op. The flag is NOT propagated through the parent-first cascade. (3) Help and docs: the real help sources are src/rebar/_cli/help/edit.txt and src/rebar/_cli/help/claim.txt; docs/cli-reference.md is generated by scripts/gen_cli_reference.py and is regenerated, not hand-edited. Both help texts state the flags are not atomic against concurrent store reconvergence and point at `review-plan --status`. Exception path: if review_plan RAISES (provider outage, config error) instead of returning a verdict dict, both flags let the exception propagate to the standard CLI error handler — for edit --review the EDIT remains committed (it landed before the review started) and the process exits via the normal error path; for claim --review the claim core is never invoked. A test covers a raising stub for each flag. Lock discipline: neither flag holds the store flock across the review — the edit/claim appends its own event under the normal short-lived lock, releases it, and only then invokes review_plan, which itself takes the lock only for the brief under-lock generation re-check at signing; the multi-minute LLM passes run with no lock held. Both flags are CLI-only (the MCP surface keeps its REBAR_MCP_ALLOW_LLM fence). Alternative rejected: new fused verbs — no OSS precedent, larger surface.\n\n## Scope\nsrc/rebar/_commands/composer.py, src/rebar/_commands/claim.py, src/rebar/_commands/gates.py (extract _plan_review_gate_applies; precheck refactored to call it), src/rebar/_cli/help/edit.txt, src/rebar/_cli/help/claim.txt, docs/cli-reference.md (regenerated via scripts/gen_cli_reference.py), docs/exit-codes.md (document the --review exit codes for edit and claim — the new codes apply only when the flag is passed; the flagless contracts are unchanged), tests/unit/test_review_flags.py (new).\n\n## Testing\nUnit with a stubbed review_plan returning verdict dicts: bare `--review` parses without consuming a following token (an edit with `--review --priority 1` keeps both); edit --review runs review after the EDIT commit and maps PASS/BLOCK/INDETERMINATE stubs to exits 0/1/2; a BLOCK leaves the edit committed; claim --review claims on a PASS stub, and on BLOCK, INDETERMINATE, and retryable-degrade stubs never calls the claim core and exits 1, 2, and 11 respectively; it prints the gate-disabled notice for a bug-type ticket and claims anyway; it fails closed when the post-review recheck still reports stale; the parent cascade never receives the flag; a review stub that itself acquires the store flock succeeds under both flags; a RAISING review stub leaves the edit committed (edit --review) and never invokes the claim core (claim --review), exiting through the standard CLI error path.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Bare --review parses as a valueless flag without swallowing the next token (checked: parser unit test).\n- [ ] edit --review runs the review strictly after the EDIT commit and exits with _disposition_exit_code(result, indeterminate_code=2) (checked: unit test recording call order and exit codes for PASS/BLOCK/INDETERMINATE stubs).\n- [ ] claim --review claims only on PASS; on BLOCK/INDETERMINATE/retryable-degrade it never invokes the claim core and exits 1/2/11 with the review summary printed (checked: unit tests with stubbed verdicts, including a retryable stub, asserting the claim core is not called).\n- [ ] Both flag handlers obtain _disposition_exit_code via the lazy in-function import and the review-plan CLI's own exit-code behavior is unchanged (checked: unit test asserting the mapped exit codes; existing review-plan CLI exit-code tests pass).\n- [ ] claim --review senses applicability via the shared _plan_review_gate_applies helper (also used by precheck), reviews only when the gate applies AND claim_gate_check reports not-ok, prints the skip notice when the gate does not apply, and never propagates through the parent cascade (checked: unit tests, including a config-disabled case and an exempt-type case).\n- [ ] Help sources document non-atomicity and reference review-plan --status, and docs/cli-reference.md is regenerated (checked: help-text assertions; regenerated file committed).\n- [ ] docs/exit-codes.md documents the --review exit codes for edit and claim and states the flagless contracts are unchanged (checked: doc text assertion; existing exit-code conformance tests pass).\n- [ ] The store lock is not held while the review runs: a review stub that acquires the store flock succeeds under both flags (checked: unit test).\n- [ ] A raising review_plan propagates through the standard CLI error path with the edit still committed and the claim never attempted (checked: unit tests with a raising stub for each flag).","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/composer.py","reason":"edit --review valueless flag"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/claim.py","reason":"claim_compute review parameter"},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/help/edit.txt","reason":"help text"},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/help/claim.txt","reason":"help text"},{"path":"docs/cli-reference.md","reason":"regenerated"},{"path":"docs/exit-codes.md","reason":"--review exit codes"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_review_flags.py","reason":"new tests"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["parent","a492-3e46-ca44-40a5"],["relates_to","d33d-bf91-2086-4b40"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"a492-3e46-ca44-40a5","parent_status_uuid":"904afcbb-c742-4239-80b4-f98c50a4c2eb","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"sta